:: Junction
(set: $thud_lvl to 2)
The crawlway opens into a wide natural cavern. Water has carved the walls into smooth, rippling folds. The heartbeat is clearer here, rising from somewhere below.

(display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

To one side, a [[low doorway->Pump Room]] leads into a room full of pipes. Opposite it, a [[brick archway->Cistern]] smells of standing water.
(if: $collapsing)[The crawlway behind you has collapsed into a wall of rubble.]\
(else:)[[[Climb back up the crawlway->Crawlway3]]]


:: Pump Room
(set: $thud_lvl to 2)
Rusted pipes crowd this low room, running from a great iron hand-pump into the wall toward the cistern. Water drips steadily from a cracked joint overhead.

|wheelspot>[(if: $wheel_stuck)[A (link-repeat: "valve wheel")[(replace: ?wheelresult)[($useOn: "the rusted valve wheel", (dm: "hammer", "use-hammer-wheel"), "You heave at the wheel, but it is rusted solid to the pipe.")(rerun: ?wheelspot)]] is rusted onto the end of a dead pipe.]]
|wheelresult>[]
(if: $where's sandbag is "Pump Room")[A sandbag slumps beneath the dripping joint.]<sandbag|
(click-replace: ?sandbag)[You heave the sandbag onto your shoulder.($move: "sandbag", "player")]

Scratched into the pump housing is a ($reveal: "pump-mark", "mark", ": ''a single notch beside a wavy line''").

(display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

[[Back to the cavern->Junction]]


:: use-hammer-wheel [use]
(set: $wheel_stuck to false)($move: "valve-wheel", "player")\
*Clang!* The rust gives way, and the valve wheel drops into your hands.


:: Cistern
(set: $thud_lvl to 2)
|cisternspot>[(if: not $cistern_drained)[Black water fills this vaulted brick tank to chest height. Its surface trembles faintly with every heartbeat. An empty (link-repeat: "valve stem")[(replace: ?cisternresult)[($useOn: "the valve stem", (dm: "valve-wheel", "use-wheel-stem"), "That doesn't fit the square stem.")(rerun: ?cisternspot)]] pokes out of the wall beside the archway.]\
(else:)[The drained tank drips and echoes. Silt coats the brick floor. A flight of stone stairs, hidden until now, leads [[down into the dark->Weighing Room]]. Above, iron rungs climb a narrow [[drain shaft->Wine Cellar]].

Scratched into the floor of the tank is a ($reveal: "cistern-mark", "mark", ": ''two notches beside a branching root''").]]
|cisternresult>[]

(display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

[[Back to the cavern->Junction]]


:: use-wheel-stem [use]
($move: "valve-wheel", "gone")(set: $cistern_drained to true)\
You fit the valve wheel onto the stem and heave. It turns with a groan, and somewhere below, a sluice opens. With a deep gurgle, the water drains away.


:: Weighing Room
(set: $thud_lvl to 3)
A square chamber of fitted stone. An iron portcullis bars the passage onward, and a broad pressure plate is set into the floor before it.

<!-- The portcullis is open while any item rests here (on the plate); there is no separate flag. -->\
|platespot>[(set: _onPlate to (find: _x where $where's (_x) is "Weighing Room", ...(dm-names: $where)))\
(if: _onPlate's length is 0)[The (link-repeat: "pressure plate")[(replace: ?plateresult)[\
<!-- Any carried item tagged "heavy" works. -->\
(set: _heavy to (dm:))\
(for: each _x, ...($carried:))[(if: (passage: _x + "-item")'s tags contains "heavy")[(set: _heavy to it + (dm: _x, "use-plate"))]]\
($useOn: "the pressure plate", _heavy, "You set it on the plate, but nothing happens. It needs something heavier.")(rerun: ?platespot)]] sits level with the floor. The portcullis is down.]\
(else:)[The (print: ($name: _onPlate's 1st)) rests on the sunken pressure plate, and the portcullis hangs raised on its chains. (link-repeat: "Take back the " + ($name: _onPlate's 1st))[(replace: ?plateresult)[($move: _onPlate's 1st, "player")The plate rises, and the portcullis crashes down.(rerun: ?platespot)]]

[[Duck under the portcullis->Echo Fork]]]]
|plateresult>[]

(display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

[[Climb the stairs->Cistern]]


:: use-plate [use]
($move: $used_item, "Weighing Room")\
You set the (print: ($name: $used_item)) on the plate. It sinks with a heavy ''clunk'', and the portcullis grinds upward on its chains.
